  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best (config_033: scvi_n200, ResNet50, transformer, weighted, 0.713) has been built by sequentially optimizing RNA encoder, profile setting, aggregation, and fusion. The one major axis still unexplored in this best configuration is the image encoder architecture—we have only ever used ResNet50, which produced very weak image-only performance (0.208). Config_039 swaps only the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) constant, giving a clean single-variable comparison. This tests whether the modest ~0.9-pt multimodal gain over RNA-only is an artifact of a weak image encoder or reflects a fundamental ceiling on image signal. A strong positive result would identify a new exploitable axis; a null result would confirm that further image-encoder investment is unlikely to help and redirect budget toward RNA-encoder alternatives (e.g., scgpt) or other structural changes. Under the limited budget, this is the highest-information next step because it resolves uncertainty on an entirely untested axis while remaining a direct exploitation of the current best configuration."
}

